{
  "step_1": "The decision reason evaluates the lotteries based on their maximum and minimum outcomes. Lottery A has a maximum outcome of 3000 Euros and a minimum outcome of 0 Euros. Lottery B has a maximum outcome of 6000 Euros and a minimum outcome of 0 Euros. The reason prefers the lottery with the more favorable maximum outcome; if those are equal, it considers the minimum outcome. Here, the maximum outcome of B (6000) is greater than that of A (3000), so according to the reason, B should be preferred. The relevant information (outcomes and their probabilities) is fully available and clearly defined in the lotteries.",
