{
  "step_1": "The decision reason evaluates lotteries based on the outcomes, specifically prioritizing the maximum outcome (the worst-case loss in this context) and, if tied, the minimum outcome. In this decision problem, both lotteries have a maximum outcome of 0 Euros (no gain) and a minimum outcome of a negative amount (loss). The maximum outcome is identical for both: 0 Euros. Therefore, the decision reason would then compare the minimum outcomes (i.e., the largest losses). Lottery A has a minimum outcome of -4000 Euros (with 20% probability), and Lottery B has a minimum outcome of -3000 Euros (with 25% probability). Since -3000 is greater than -4000, Lottery B has the more favorable minimum outcome. Thus, according to the decision reason, Lottery B is preferred. The relevant information from the lotteries is fully available and can be derived: maximum outcomes are equal, minimum outcomes differ, and B has the more favorable minimum outcome.",
